<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="5">
  <Content>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>FADE IN:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>EXT. PALM BAY, FLORIDA - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Rain bands rake a street of low concrete-block houses. Hurricane shutters bolted tight. A stop sign shivers on its post.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>One window glows phone-blue.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INT. DEL'S BEDROOM - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A ceiling fan turns over a woman asleep on top of the covers in yesterday's clothes: DELPHINE "DEL" ARCENEAUX (34), Haitian-American, close-cropped natural hair, a hospital lanyard still around her neck.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>On the nightstand, face up: a phone. Beside it, a small dog-bone of steel, stretched thin at the waist and snapped in two.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The phone BUZZES.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Del is sitting up before the second buzz, the way soldiers and new mothers wake.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INSERT - PHONE SCREEN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>3:12 AM. PAGE. imaging-api: 95th percentile over 500 ms. Cape Shore Regional.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>BACK TO SCENE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She doesn't check the time. She knows the time.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(to the ceiling)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Three twelve.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She flips open a laptop on the bed. Its glow finds a wall calendar: fourteen months of pages, each one crowded with small red circles drawn at the same hour.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Graphs bloom on the screen. A line climbs, crosses a dotted red line, and keeps climbing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Come on. Come on, come on...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The line crests. Falls back under the red. Her shoulders drop an inch.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She does not lie down. She sits in the blue light, listening to the wind, waiting for the next one.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition">
      <Text>SMASH CUT TO:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Center" Type="Action">
      <Text>YIELD LIMIT LINE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>EXT. RAY'S HOUSE - MELBOURNE, FLORIDA - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A tidy stucco house under a fast grey sky. Plywood leans against the carport. The garage door is up. A radio talks to nobody.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RADIO (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>...Hurricane Lucinda, a Category 3, is forecast to stay offshore but bring tropical-storm-force winds to the Space Coast after dark. Brevard County shelters open at noon...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INT. RAY'S GARAGE WORKSHOP - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A machinist's chapel. Pegboard walls, every tool outlined in marker so its absence shows. A framed photo: a young man in coveralls, a launch tower behind him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>That man, forty years on: RAYMOND "RAY" ARCENEAUX (69), Haitian-born, white stubble, reading glasses on a cord. He holds a sheet of plywood to a window frame. Del holds the other end, a drill in her free hand, eyes half shut.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You're holding it crooked.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I'm holding it fine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You're holding it like a woman who slept two hours.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Three.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>He takes the drill from her and sinks four screws without looking. Then he looks.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Same time?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Same time.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Every night?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Most nights. Fourteen months.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And they pay you to find out why.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>They pay me to make it stop. Finding out why is extra.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Ray crosses to his bench and pulls a dust cover off a small benchtop TENSILE TESTER: a hand crank, two steel jaws, a round dial gauge with a single black needle. He clamps a fresh steel coupon between the jaws.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Come here.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Papa. I've seen it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You've seen it. Come look.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She comes. He cranks. The jaws pull. The needle climbs, smooth and steady.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Every piece of steel has a line. Up to the line, you can load her all day. Let go...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>He backs off the crank. The needle sinks to zero.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>...and she springs back like nothing happened.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>He cranks again. The needle climbs, climbs, and HESITATES: a small stutter. Then it moves on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>There. You see it? That's the yield. One hair past that...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>He lets go. The needle settles, but not at zero. A little above it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>...and she remembers. Forever.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And past that?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>He cranks. The coupon's waist narrows like pulled taffy. There is no sound in the garage but the ratchet.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>SNAP.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The halves jump in the jaws. Ray drops them in her palm. They're warm.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Past that, she don't remember nothing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Del looks down at the two pieces. She knows this lesson. She has its twin on her nightstand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Pitit mwen. You been ringing past your line a long time.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Somebody has to hold it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Thirty-one years, every part that went up off that pad crossed a bench like this one. Not one was held together by a man's hands. Every piece carried its own load, to its own line. All of them at once. That's what flies.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>My system's not a rocket.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>No. On a rocket, somebody watches all the pieces at once.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She pockets the broken halves.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INT. CAPE SHORE REGIONAL MEDICAL CENTER - THEO'S OFFICE - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Glass walls. Beyond them the Indian River Lagoon turns to pewter under the storm. Below, crews tape windows in big white Xs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>THEO VANCE (46), Vice President of Infrastructure, Air Force posture in a hospital fleece, stands by a wall screen. SLOANE MERCER (38), immaculate, tablet in hand, is finishing a pitch. Del leans in the doorway with a coffee.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The wall screen, in clean enormous type: PERIHELION. 52% FASTER. 30% OFF YOUR BILL. ZERO BABYSITTING.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SLOANE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>...which is why our agent doesn't advise your autoscaler. It replaces it. One brain, no committee. And your engineers finally sleep.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She smiles at Del. Del does not smile back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>THEO</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Del. You've had the other one on trial a week. The compass thing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Omni-Compass.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>THEO</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>What's its number?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It doesn't have one yet. It's watching.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SLOANE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(kindly)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Watching.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It sits on top of what we already run. It doesn't throw anything out. Our autoscaler stays. The cluster stays. It moves them together, every piece to its own limit and never past it. And if it's ever wrong, one switch hands everything back the way it was.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SLOANE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And how much faster is that?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I'll tell you when I have a receipt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SLOANE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>We have benchmarks.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Can I run them?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SLOANE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>They're proprietary.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A beat. Theo rubs his eyes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>THEO</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>The outpatient centers close at nine for the storm. They'll push every scan they've got to us before they lock up. And the board meets at seven tomorrow morning, storm or no storm. They want a number. A big one. With a dollar sign in front.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And if the true one's small?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>THEO</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Then bring me a small true one, and I'll lose with it. But bring me something.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INT. CAPE SHORE REGIONAL - EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT - DUSK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Stretchers line a corridor. Sandbags at the ambulance bay. Monitors chirp.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>NADIA REYES (52), charge nurse, reading glasses pushed up into her hair, wipes down a wall-mounted tracking board. She spots Del passing and aims a pen at her.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>NADIA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You. Three-twelve.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Hi, Nadia.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>NADIA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Your voice is the last thing I hear before my coffee. Two nights ago the CT viewer froze four minutes. Stroke alert on the table. Four minutes, mija.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I know. I was on the phone with you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>NADIA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I know you know. I'm telling you so you remember it tonight.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She taps the tracking board: rows of patients, and beside each a small shape. Green circles. One yellow diamond.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>NADIA (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Green, good. Yellow, coming. Red, I pray in two languages.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Tonight it's gonna be all of them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>NADIA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Then don't sleep.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>When have I ever.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>EXT. COLOCATION DATA CENTER - MELBOURNE - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Wind hammers a windowless concrete box. Rain sheets through its floodlights.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INT. COLOCATION DATA HALL - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A cold aisle of server racks, ten thousand tiny lights breathing in rhythm. Del walks it with a flashlight past a sign: GENERATOR TESTED 22:00.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>At the operations desk, a wall of monitors: THE WALL. Each screen is one muscle of the system: PODS. MACHINES. COOLING. POWER. In each corner, a light. All green circles.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>One screen stands apart: OMNI-COMPASS. WATCHING.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Del sits. She drags fourteen months of logs onto the wall. Night stacks on night like strata in a cliff.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>With a grease pencil, she draws a line on the glass at 3:00. Another at 3:05. At 3:09. At 3:12.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(to herself)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Three o'clock, the clinics send the day's scans. Three-oh-five, the autoscaler notices. Late. It asks for pods. The pods wait. There's no room. Three-oh-nine, the cluster asks for a machine. Three-twelve...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She taps 3:12.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>...me.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She scrolls on. 3:40, a machine removed. 3:52, pods evicted. 4:10, another small climb.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And then they put it all back like it never happened. Every night.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A process list. One name recurs at three o'clock: PRHL-AGENT.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Hello.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She opens it. Installed: last Tuesday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She glances at her phone's calendar. Fourteen months of red circles. The agent is one week old.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Not you. You're new.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She sits back and studies the wall. Every light green. Every muscle doing exactly its job.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Nobody's wrong. Every one of you does what you were built to do. Alone. And late.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>On a rocket, somebody watches all the pieces at once.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Yeah. Me. At three-twelve.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Every rack light in the hall goes dark.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Silence. A heartbeat. Two.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Then a deep diesel THRUM rises through the floor. The lights breathe back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>On the wall: UTILITY POWER LOST. ON GENERATOR. POWER LINE 70%.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Okay. Okay.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Her phone buzzes. Not 3:12. It's 1:58.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INSERT - PHONE SCREEN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>NADIA: Trauma inbound. Rollover on 192. CT in ten.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>BACK TO SCENE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The PODS light turns: a yellow diamond.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A new panel slides onto the wall: PERIHELION AGENT. COST MODE ON. MACHINES 9 TO 6.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>No. No, no, no. What are you doing?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She opens the agent's panel. It explains itself in a friendly font: Generator budget detected. Parking idle capacity. Projected savings 31%.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>They're not idle. They're about to work.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The MACHINES light turns to a red octagon. Then PODS. Red octagon.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INT. CAPE SHORE REGIONAL - CT ROOM - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The scanner hums. CT technologist DION PRICE (26) stares at a viewer: a spinning wheel. Nadia at his shoulder. On the table, a young man in a cervical collar, rain still on his face.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DION</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It's not loading.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>NADIA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(into her phone)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Del.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INTERCUT - DATA HALL / CT ROOM</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I see it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>NADIA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Then fix it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Their agent turned off our autoscaler. It didn't sit on top of it. It sat in its chair. And now it's saving money.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>NADIA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Tell it to spend some!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>On Del's screen, a switch drawn like a red guarded toggle: KILL SWITCH. PERIHELION AGENT.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She flips the guard and throws it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>AGENT STOPPED. NATIVE CONTROLLERS RESTORED.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The native autoscaler wakes. The PODS panel asks for more. The pods wait. Machines begin to boot. Slowly.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DION</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Still spinning.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>We're back to normal. Normal is late.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Her eyes go to the one screen that has been patient all night: OMNI-COMPASS. WATCHING.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She takes Ray's broken halves out of her pocket and sets them on the desk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>One week of trial. No receipt. A Category 3 outside.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>NADIA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(through the phone)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Del!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Del switches it. WATCHING becomes AUTOPILOT.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>ON THE WALL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Each muscle's screen becomes a gauge: one needle, one line. The generator's 70% is drawn as a hard edge.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The needles rise. PODS. MACHINES. COOLING. POWER. Each toward its own line.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Each needle reaches its line. And holds. Not one hair past.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The lights turn. Red octagon to yellow diamond. Yellow diamond to green circle. One by one.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(barely a whisper)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Every piece to its own line.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INT. CT ROOM - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The wheel stops. An image fills the viewer: the young man's spine, clean and whole.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DION</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>We're up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>NADIA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(into the phone, breathing again)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>We're up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INT. COLOCATION DATA HALL - LATER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The wall clock reads 4:40. On every screen, green circles. Del's phone BUZZES.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She tenses. Reads.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INSERT - PHONE SCREEN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>PAGE. node-14: disk failing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>BACK TO SCENE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She almost laughs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>That one's real.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She takes a flashlight and a replacement drive and walks into the cold aisle to do her job.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>EXT. INDIAN RIVER LAGOON - CAUSEWAY - DAWN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The storm has gone north. A scrubbed pink sky. Palm fronds strewn across the causeway. Utility linemen ride bucket trucks up to the wires. A line of brown pelicans skims the flat water.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INT. DEL'S CAR - PARKED ON THE CAUSEWAY - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A laptop balanced on the steering wheel. On it, a grid of video tiles: the board. Theo in his office. Sloane in a hotel room. GLORIA HAYWOOD (74), retired structures engineer, in a Titusville kitchen while a roof tarp snaps outside her window. Three more members, coffee in hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>THEO (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Two trials, one night. Sloane.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SLOANE (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Overnight, on generator power, our agent cut compute cost thirty-one percent. That's the number.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>GLORIA (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Between what hours?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SLOANE (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Between about one and four.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Theo lifts a printout.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>THEO (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Emergency department log. CT viewer unavailable from one fifty-eight to two sixteen. Trauma patient on the table.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Silence on the call. Sloane's face doesn't move.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SLOANE (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Our agent responded to the budget it was given. And hers ran more machines than ours. It burned more fuel.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It did. That's power given. It bought a scan.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>GLORIA (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Cheap is easy at two in the morning. Cheap with nobody hurt is the job.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>THEO (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Del. Your number.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Del's phone lights on the dashboard: a slide from Theo's analyst. OMNI-COMPASS: 44% FASTER. In small print beneath: our model.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She looks at it for a long second. Deletes it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I've got one number, and it isn't from last night.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>THEO (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Go.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Last night was one night. One night is a story. Their record is thirteen Kubernetes tests, each one run three times. Count the pages a person would have been sent. Native: thirteen point eight. With it on top: ten point three. A quarter fewer. In all three runs. Every row of it has a receipt, and every receipt has a run number.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SLOANE (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And the bill?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Inside the noise. Nobody's measured your bill. If anybody tells you they did in one night, ask them for the receipt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>GLORIA (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(a small smile)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>At the Cape we didn't fly on one test.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Three runs is a receipt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Beat. Theo looks from tile to tile.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>THEO (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Sloane. Can we run your benchmark?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SLOANE (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I can send you a summary.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>THEO (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>That's a no.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>GLORIA (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I move we extend the compass trial ninety days. And Ms. Arceneaux brings us the next receipt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>THEO (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Second?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Hands rise in the tiles. Some still holding coffee.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The tiles blink out one by one until two remain. Del. Sloane.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SLOANE (ON SCREEN)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Off the record. How do you sleep, doing it your way?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Ask me tomorrow.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Sloane almost smiles. Her tile goes dark.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INT. RAY'S GARAGE WORKSHOP - MORNING</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Ray pushes an inch of rainwater out under the door with a squeegee. The plywood held. The radio murmurs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Del comes in, keys in hand, eyes red.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Well?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Ninety days.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>That's a yes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>That's a "bring us the next receipt."</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>That's the only yes there is.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She crosses to the tensile tester. Takes a fresh coupon from the drawer and clamps it in. Ray leans on the squeegee and watches.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She cranks. The needle climbs. Climbs. Hesitates: the yield.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She stops. Backs the crank off.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The needle sinks to zero.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Springs back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You found your line.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She lays the broken halves on the bench beside the whole one. Then she lies down on the old couch along the wall, boots still on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>RAY (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(soft)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Dòmi, pitit.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Her phone BUZZES on her chest. Her whole body flinches.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INSERT - PHONE SCREEN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>NADIA: a photo of the emergency department's tracking board, every shape a green circle. One word under it: sleep.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>BACK TO SCENE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Del smiles. She turns the phone face down on her chest and closes her eyes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The radio says the sun is out over Cocoa Beach. Ray lays a blanket over her and goes back to the water.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition">
      <Text>FADE OUT.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Center" Type="Action">
      <Text>The pages a person would be sent: down 25.7%, GAIN in all three of our runs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Center" Type="Action">
      <Text>Thirteen Kubernetes tests, real software on GitHub's machines, omni-v21. Receipt: results/OVERSIGHT_PAGES.md.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Center" Type="Action">
      <Text>The characters, the hospital, the vendor and the storm are fictional. Omni-Compass is real, and every number it speaks here has its receipt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Center" Type="Action">
      <Text>THE END</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="General">
      <Text>© 2026 The Omni-Compass LLC. All rights reserved. Evaluation and Simulation use only. Any commercial use, commercialization, monetization, production use, redistribution or hosted service of any part of Omni-Compass requires a signed, paid Omni-Compass Enterprise License from The Omni-Compass LLC. Every copy, export, report and printout carries this notice with LICENSE, NOTICE and DISCLOSURES.md. All patents, copyrights and trademarks filed in the USA. www.omni-compass.com</Text>
    </Paragraph>
  </Content>
  <TitlePage>
    <Content>
      <Paragraph Alignment="Center" Type="Text">
      <Text>YIELD LIMIT LINE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
      <Paragraph Alignment="Center" Type="Text">
      <Text>an original screenplay by</Text>
    </Paragraph>
      <Paragraph Alignment="Center" Type="Text">
      <Text>The Omni-Compass LLC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
      <Paragraph Alignment="Center" Type="Text">
      <Text>From the published record of Omni-Compass. Every number spoken in it has its receipt (docs/film/production.json, checked by tools/film.py).</Text>
    </Paragraph>
      <Paragraph Alignment="Left" Type="Text">
      <Text>4 November 2026</Text>
    </Paragraph>
      <Paragraph Alignment="Left" Type="Text">
      <Text>The Omni-Compass LLC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
      <Paragraph Alignment="Left" Type="Text">
      <Text>Main office infrastructure, toll-free direct 1-888-339-9551</Text>
    </Paragraph>
      <Paragraph Alignment="Left" Type="Text">
      <Text>System route asset 1-888-DEX-YLL-1</Text>
    </Paragraph>
      <Paragraph Alignment="Left" Type="Text">
      <Text>Florida landline 321-746-4411</Text>
    </Paragraph>
      <Paragraph Alignment="Left" Type="Text">
      <Text>www.omni-compass.com</Text>
    </Paragraph>
      <Paragraph Alignment="Left" Type="Text">
      <Text>© 2026 The Omni-Compass LLC. All rights reserved. Evaluation and Simulation use only. Any commercial use, commercialization, monetization, production use, redistribution or hosted service of any part of Omni-Compass requires a signed, paid Omni-Compass Enterprise License from The Omni-Compass LLC. Every copy, export, report and printout carries this notice with LICENSE, NOTICE and DISCLOSURES.md. All patents, copyrights and trademarks filed in the USA. www.omni-compass.com</Text>
    </Paragraph>
      <Paragraph Alignment="Left" Type="Text">
      <Text>The characters, Cape Shore Regional Medical Center, the vendor Perihelion and Hurricane Lucinda are fictional. The places are real: Palm Bay, Melbourne, the Indian River Lagoon, US 192, Titusville and Cocoa Beach, on Florida's Space Coast. Omni-Compass is real, and is shown as it works: on top of the controllers a system already runs, never in their place.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    </Content>
